TO MANIPULATE CSS WITH JQUERY


$("h1").css("color", "green");



$("h1").addClass("big-title");
EXAMPLE WITH A PREDEFINED CLASS


$("h1").addClass("big-title margin50 coursive");


ADD TEXT



$("h1").text("Hello, jQuery!");
//HTML METHOD
$("button").html("<em>DON'T Click me!</em>");


MANIPULATING ATTRIBUTES

console.log($('img').attr('src')); // Consulting attributes


$('a').attr('href', "https://espanol.yahoo.com/") // Manipulating Attributes


ADDING EVENT LISTENERS

$("h1").click(function() {
    $("h1").css("color", "purple");
});

TRADITIONAL WAY TO MANIPULATE BUTTONS (IN THIS EXAMPLE THE BUTTONS ARE GOING TO MAKE THE COLOR TO CHANGE)

for (var i = 0; i<5; i++) {
    document.querySelectorAll("button")[i].addEventListener("click", function() {
        document.querySelector("h1").style.color = "purple";
    });
    }

JQUERY METHOD WITH BUTTONS


$("button").click(function() {
    $("h1").css("color", "purple");
});

// IN THE EXAMPLE ABOVE IT WAS SETTED AN INPUT WHEN THE UX TYPES IN THE INPUT THE TITLE GETS MODIFIED
$('input').keypress(function (event) {
    $('h1').text(event.key);   
});


// method for adding functions
$("h1").on("click", function() {
    $("h1").css("color", "red");
});



JQUERY ADDING ELEMENTS 

$("h1").before("<h2>jQuery</h2>");

$("h1").after("<h2>jQuery</h2>");


$("h1").prepend("<h2>jQuery</h2>"); // it is added inside the element selected after the $, it will be displayed before the element selected (part of the Content of the element selected)

$("h1").append("<h2>jQuery</h2>");// it is added inside the element selected after the $, it will be displayed at the last part of the closing element selected (Part of the Content of the element selected)

JQUERY REMOVE ELEMENTS 

$("button").remove();

WEBSITE ANIMATIONS WITH JQUERY

$("button").on("click", function() {
    $("h1").hide();
});

// Makes the event goes front way and backway
$("button").on("click", function() {
    $("h1").toggle();
});

//FADE

$("button").on("click", function() {
    $("h1").fadeOut();
    //$("h1").fadeIn();
});

$("button").on("click", function() {
    $("h1").fadeToggle();
});

// Slide

$("button").on("click", function() {
    $("h1").slideUp().slideDown();
});


$("button").on("click", function() {
    $("h1").slideToggle();
});

// Animate only for numeric values

$("button").on("click", function() {
    $("h1").animate({opacity: 0.5});
});



